<Base title="Synvel">
  <p class="meta"><a href="/projects/">← Projects</a></p>
  <h1>Synvel</h1>
  <p><span class="badge seed">in design</span></p>
  <p>
    Synthetic Virtual Environment Lifeform. A system that uses an LLM as a thinking piece,
    but not the focus: the brain is one organ of many, and it's swappable, so as newer and
    better models come out nothing else has to be modified.
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>Memory: a large plain-text knowledge base, read at every session start.</li>
    <li>Feeling layer: a small monitor that watches for patterns in the record and pushes back.</li>
    <li>Senses: a separate project called Sylas, the eyes, ears, and mouth.</li>
    <li>Self-learning proof: a small local model trained on my own writing, retrained from my edits.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>Roots in Brooks' subsumption architecture and Friston's active inference. Build notes are in the <a href="/log/">devlog</a> as they happen.</p>
</Base>
